{"kind": "textbox", "slide": 5, "id": "code", "bbox": [1.75, 1.95, 5.5, 4.1], "text": "interface SettlementBoundary {\n  canonical(order: PartnerOrder): Order;\n  canonical(entry: LedgerRow): LedgerEntry;\n  emit(event: BoundaryEvent): void;\n}\n\n// Four concepts. One owner.\n// Changing a field is one review,\n// not six.", "role": "body", "style": {"fontFace": "IBM Plex Mono", "fontSize": 12, "color": "17191C", "lineSpacingMultiple": 1.35}}
{"kind": "textbox", "slide": 5, "id": "margin-1", "bbox": [8.2, 1.95, 4.2, 1.2], "text": "Nothing above the boundary changes on day one. Adapters keep running and are retired one at a time.", "styleRef": "ledger-row", "role": "body", "style": {"fontSize": 14}}
{"kind": "textbox", "slide": 5, "id": "margin-2", "bbox": [8.2, 3.45, 4.2, 1.2], "text": "The contract is versioned. A breaking change is a review, and the review is the point.", "styleRef": "ledger-row", "role": "body", "style": {"fontSize": 14}}
{"kind": "textbox", "slide": 5, "id": "margin-3", "bbox": [8.2, 4.95, 4.2, 1.0], "text": "Retirement order is in the appendix; it follows incident frequency, not team preference.", "styleRef": "margin-note", "role": "caption"}
{"kind": "notes", "slide": 5, "notes": ["If anyone asks 'what exactly are we funding' — this slide."]}
{"kind": "slide", "slide": 6, "freeform": true, "id": "ask", "semanticKind": "decision", "title": "What we are asking for", "designIntent": "One sentence, then three commitments in a table. The deck ends on an obligation, not a thank-you.", "composition": "A single sentence at the top measure; a three-row table sitting at the foot of the page."}
{"kind": "textbox", "slide": 6, "id": "rail-6", "bbox": [0.55, 0.78, 0.7, 0.35], "text": "08", "styleRef": "rail-number", "role": "caption", "layer": "rail"}
{"kind": "textbox", "slide": 6, "id": "ask", "bbox": [1.45, 0.75, 10.4, 1.55], "text": "Approve one boundary, funded for two quarters, with adapter retirement gated on incident rate.", "role": "title", "style": {"fontFace": "IBM Plex Sans", "fontSize": 34, "color": "17191C", "bold": true, "lineSpacingMultiple": 1.15}}
{"kind": "connector", "slide": 6, "id": "rule-ask", "bbox": [1.45, 2.55, 10.4, 0], "style": {"color": "0B5FA5", "width": 2, "arrow": false}}
{"kind": "table", "slide": 6, "id": "commitments", "bbox": [1.45, 3.0, 10.4, 2.6], "table": {"headers": ["Commitment", "Owner", "Gate"], "rows": [["Boundary in production behind a flag", "Platform", "End of Q3"], ["First two adapters retired", "Platform + Billing", "Integration incidents below 4/quarter"], ["Remaining four retired", "Platform", "Contract stable for two quarters"]], "columnWidths": [5.0, 2.8, 2.6]}}
{"kind": "textbox", "slide": 6, "id": "close", "bbox": [1.45, 5.95, 10.4, 0.5], "text": "If the incident gate is not met, the remaining adapters stay. That is the deal.", "styleRef": "ledger-row", "role": "body"}
{"kind": "notes", "slide": 6, "notes": ["End on the gate. It is what makes this reversible."], "sources": [{"label": "Incident review log, 12 months"}]}
